Devops Interview
=====================
☁️ AWS
• EC2 CPU suddenly reaches 100% — how would you troubleshoot?
• EC2 is running but SSH isn't working — what would you check?
• ALB starts returning 5xx errors — how would you identify the root cause?
• Application works internally but not from the internet — how would you troubleshoot?


☸️ Kubernetes
• Pod is stuck in Pending — what would you check?
• Pod is in CrashLoopBackOff — how would you troubleshoot?
• Pod is running but Service isn't accessible — what's your approach?
• New deployment breaks production — how would you rollback?


🔄 CI/CD
• Pipeline succeeds but the new version isn't deployed — how would you debug?
• Production deployment fails halfway — what's your rollback strategy?
• How would you securely manage secrets?
• How would you implement Blue-Green/Canary deployment?


🏗️ Terraform
• terraform plan shows unexpected changes — what would you investigate?
• Someone manually changes Terraform-managed infrastructure — what happens?
• How would you manage state for multiple engineers?
• How would you structure dev/staging/prod?


🐧 Linux
• Production server becomes slow — how do you identify CPU/memory/disk/network issues?
• Disk reaches 100% — how would you find and safely remove the cause?
• Process is consuming high CPU — which commands would you use?
• Service is running but not listening on the expected port — how would you troubleshoot?
💡 Biggest takeaway:
Don't prepare only for:
❌ What is Kubernetes?
❌ What is Terraform?
❌ What is a Security Group?
Prepare for:
✅ Production is down. What do you check first?
✅ Which commands/tools do you use?
✅ How do you find the root cause?
✅ How do you fix it safely?
✅ How do you prevent it from happening again?
